    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0110" n="100" xml:id="pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European Advisory Commission/11–2044:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Representative to the French Provisional
                        Government</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-20T16:00:00+01:00">November 20,
                            1944—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>594. In a note signed by Bidault dated November 17, 1944<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d74-f1"/> which I have just received, the Provisional Government
                    formally accepts the invitation conveyed to it on November 11 to become a
                    permanent member of the European Advisory Commission.<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d74-f2"/> The note states in part that the Provisional Government
                    appreciates the full value of the invitation and requests me to transmit its
                    acceptance to the Government of the United States, copy of note being
                    transmitted by despatch.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d74-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d74-f1" n="27" xml:id="d74-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d74-f2" n="28" xml:id="d74-f2-content">
                <p>René Massigli, French Ambassador in the United Kingdom, was designated French
                    Representative to the European Advisory Commission and took his seat in the
                    Commission for the first time at the formal meeting held on November 27,
                    1944.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d74-f3" n="29" xml:id="d74-f3-content">
                <p>Despatch 194, November 20, 1944, not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
